# F9 — Remediation log

2026-07-12 — Discovered during P8 deploy-artifact build: `cargo build --release
--target musl -p trustchain --bin trustchain_ca` failed with
`target trustchain_ca requires the features: localhost-testing`. Traced to
`trustchain/Cargo.toml:167` (`required-features = ["localhost-testing"]`) and 3
runtime `StateProof::new_for_testing()` calls in `trustchain_ca.rs` (395, 398, 558).
Confirmed the live remote runs `trustchain_ca --production` as `trustchain.service`.

2026-07-12 — Verified production-clean alternatives: `grep -c new_for_testing` = 0
for `trustchain-stoq-server`, `trustchain-http3-server`, `trustchain-bootstrap`.

2026-07-12 — Decision (user): dual-CA split — http3-server = clearnet/gateway CA
(8444), stoq-server = node-to-node CA (8445). Deploy scope = all running+enabled.

2026-07-12 — Config work: found `.api.port` maps to the `[api]` section; the stale
`production.toml` has none → would default to port 8080 + TLS-off +
`StateRequirements::localhost_testing()` (an F9-class regression). Also confirmed
`production.toml`'s table layout does not deserialize into the current
`TrustChainConfig` (all fields required, no serde defaults). Generated both CA
configs by serializing `TrustChainConfig::production()` with `[api]` port/TLS
overrides; round-tripped through `TrustChainConfig::load()` to confirm each yields
the intended port and production State bar.

2026-07-12 — Committed `452c01aa` (config + systemd + deploy + F9 audit),
`2d9932e1` (gateway unit/config fixes surfaced during cutover). Pushed to main.

